From 332672e841804673728e70f5a9bad8bd58b28629 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vincent Leon <leon@mbp.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 14:29:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] feat(app): group the sidebar by activity

Add an Activity grouping mode next to Project and Status. Live work keeps
its status buckets at the top: needs input, failed, ready to review and
working. Below them, workspaces that finished within a chosen window
(3 hours, 12 hours or today, from local midnight) share one Done group,
and everything that finished earlier folds into one group per project,
most recently finished project first.

The window lives with the grouping mode in the sidebar view store and is
picked from a Done within row that appears in the display menu only in
activity grouping. The grouping reads the shared minute clock only in this
mode, so finished work moves out of Done as time passes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
